Prolog syntax highlighting

Converted from support/Prolog.YAML-tmLanguage in alnkpa/sublimeprolog at:
https://github.com/alnkpa/sublimeprolog/tree/9e8e142e55557465511338d5b26ca585cb729310

The converted grammar and its modifications are available under MPL-2.0 in
assets/syntaxes/02_Extra/Prolog/Prolog.sublime-syntax in the corresponding bat
release source, available from https://github.com/sharkdp/bat/releases.

Changes: convert TextMate patterns to Sublime syntax contexts, use the name
Prolog, retain the existing Perl extension association, and match decimal
numbers before integers. The full Mozilla Public License 2.0 is in LICENSE.
